{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_sdvjs2attndhuhzhbomb55avhde7vhifqqiohot5x33tfv46bnoq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All phases complete and verified from a clean tree. Final summary:\n\n## What I found and did\n\nThe prior translation was a **single-binary, `Vec`-based** Rust program: it exported **0 of the C's 19 symbols** and hand-emulated `strtol`/`fgets`. That made FFI-level differential testing impossible, so I restructured it into an ABI-faithful `cdylib` + `rlib` (`src/lib.rs`, 927 lines) whose `#[no_mangle] extern \"C\" fn main` is *also* the `driver` binary's entry point (`src/main.rs` is a `#![no_main]` shim) — exactly like the C build.\n\n**Phase A artifacts** (`SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`) — derived mechanically from the C:\n- No cargo `[features]`, no CMake options, no `#ifdef` → **exactly one build configuration** (`cargo check --no-default-features` == default, both clean).\n- **19/19 symbols** exported by the C `.so` are exported by the Rust `.so`; symbol diff empty; 0 undefined non-libc symbols.\n- ERRORS.md: 57 rows (all 12 `run_engine` error codes, every `iv_*`/`prog_fetch` rejection, negative-input branches, CLI rejections). 55 have passing tests; the 2 remaining are marked n/a because the C performs *no* check there (raw NULL struct deref / oversized `n` = UB, not a rejection).\n- CONFIGS.md: 65 rows, all passing.\n\n**Phases B–C** — 59 tests (`tests/differential.rs`, `tests/cli.rs`) that load **both `.so`s via `libloading`** (private per-test copies so the C `static`s start pristine) plus 130 shell CLI cases. Run against **both** the release and the debug cdylib (debug enables Rust's overflow checks — nothing panicked, confirming every wrap is intentional).\n\n**C quirks reproduced, not fixed** (each covered by a test): `process_a_stream` always returns `INT_MIN` (the `size_t` vs `-0x80000000LL` comparison), opcode 9's double-pop, `(size_t)k` rejecting negative jumps, opcode 7 swallowing inner errors as trace `12`, an empty argv string pushing `0`, and `iv_reserve`'s `nc*sizeof(int)` wrapping to 0 so `realloc(p,0)` frees the buffer.\n\n**Mutation testing** exposed a real blind spot: injecting `iv_reserve`: *start doubling at 8 instead of `v->cap`* **survived**, because through the public API `cap` is always `8·2^k`. I added rows 27b/27c/51b, which hand the library a caller-`malloc`ed vector with e.g. `cap == 10` — they kill it. 11 other mutations were each caught by 10–26 tests.\n\n```\nALL VERIFICATION STEPS PASSED     (scripts/run_all.sh, from rm -rf target c_src/build)\n  cargo check/build/test × 1 feature combination   57 → 59 tests ok\n  differential suite vs DEBUG cdylib               59 tests ok\n  symbol parity                                    19/19, 0 missing\n  shell CLI differential                           130/130 cases matched\n```\n\n`c_src/` sources are untouched (only the `build/` output directory was added, as the instructions specified)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1779,"cache_read_input_tokens":299654,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1779,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3ae6ba8e-9c81-4b9f-bd39-3ec717477d24","uuid":"ac8253d3-d854-4408-a4ff-89c3eba6a368","timestamp":"2026-08-20T01:01:00.542Z"}
